WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.670
Here's how to play a game controller as a MIDI device in PadForge.

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.830
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.490
This MIDI controller came from Add Controller's music note,

4
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.240
with a DualSense assigned.

5
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:14.420
Open it.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.990
The bar at the top sets the channel, how many sliders and notes it sends,

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.750
where they start, and how hard each note plays.

8
00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.485
The sticks and triggers send Control Change messages.

9
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:30.015
These bars move as the pad's sticks do.

10
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.940
The buttons play notes, starting at middle C.

11
00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:39.095
In your music app, pick PadForge's MIDI port as an input.

12
00:00:39.645 --> 00:00:41.855
The port needs Windows MIDI Services,

13
00:00:42.185 --> 00:00:46.095
and its card in Settings installs it on a PC that doesn't have it.

14
00:00:46.565 --> 00:00:50.455
Without it, an Output Port picker sends to a port you already have.

15
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.380
Find more guides at padforge.org.
